<h2>Purpose</h2>
<p>
  Grounds decision
  <a href="/backlog/3144-curate-the-constitution-tier-s-full-principle-set-and-quanti/">#3144</a>, which turns
  <a href="/backlog/2564-adopt-spec-based-programming-across-the-constellation-schema/">#2564</a>&rsquo;s Fork 5
  &mdash; a <em>substantively entrenched</em> constitutional-amendment gate &mdash; from three qualitative
  clauses into buildable quantities. The three clauses are: <strong>(i)</strong> exempt from the ordinary
  supersede-with-lineage path (#911), <strong>(ii)</strong> a cooling period &ldquo;measured in days, not
  sessions,&rdquo; and <strong>(iii)</strong> a committed external artifact carrying the amendment diff and its
  red-team transcript. None of the three carried a number, a format, or a mechanism.
</p>
<p>
  The survey covers three families: mandated waiting periods in software governance, entrenchment devices in
  constitutional law, and durable-record conventions. It also checks the empirical literature on whether a
  cooling period does anything &mdash; because a default resting on &ldquo;reflection improves the call&rdquo;
  would not survive its own evidence base.
</p>

<h2>Mandated waiting periods in software governance</h2>
<p>
  The attested band is narrow, and almost nobody explains their number.
</p>
